# Python bytecode. NOT merely noise here. When the guard still carried a real denylist, a
# compiled copy of scripts/check_no_internal_info.py embedded those literals -- host
# codenames, the infra domain, a personal name -- in a binary nobody reads in review, and one
# was tracked in this PUBLIC repo before this file existed. The guard is shapes-only now and
# the tests pin that, so the specific leak is gone; the rule stays, because a .pyc of anything
# here is still an unreviewable binary in a public tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Local env / secrets. Nothing here should ever carry a value, but be explicit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
